<rml>
<head>
    <title>Letter</title>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="base.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="letter_read.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/template" href="window_shell.rml"/>
</head>
<!-- The whole window is drawn here, in the main context, like every other window of this family --
     the portrait included. #photo_image is a native render target (UI::RmlBridge::RenderTarget):
     CUIPhotoViewer draws the character into a texture exactly this element's size, so it stands at
     this document's own depth like any other image -- under a window that covers this one, beneath
     the "?" and the help drawn over it.

     #photo_slot paints the well and carries the viewer's input, since a press over a document never
     reaches the legacy mouse globals -- see PhotoViewerControl.h, which also sizes the target to
     #photo_image and points it there. #photo_help is the "?", .active while its help is open; the
     help itself is the shared tooltip. #photo_slot.webzen shows Webzen's logo in place of a sender.
     #frame_fill is the panel's own fill; each theme decides whether it needs it. #drag_strip is the
     title strip, since window_shell's rail is the banner art's full height and reaches over the
     content.

     Handlers are data-event-*, never on*: on* is RmlUi's inline script event and this build has no
     script interpreter, so those bind to nothing at all and fail silently. -->
<body template="window_shell" data-model="letter_read">
    <div id="frame_fill"></div>
    <div id="drag_strip"></div>
    <div id="window_controls">
        <button id="btn_minimize" data-event-click="letter_action('minimize')"></button>
        <button id="btn_close_x" data-event-click="letter_action('close')"></button>
    </div>
    <div id="header">{{header}}</div>
    <div id="body_pane" class="scroll-pane">
        <div class="line" data-for="line : lines">{{line.text}}</div>
    </div>
    <div id="photo_slot"><img id="photo_image"/><div id="photo_help"></div></div>
    <div id="footer">
        <button class="btn" data-event-click="letter_action('reply')">{{reply_label}}</button><button class="btn" data-event-click="letter_action('delete')">{{delete_label}}</button><button class="btn narrow" data-event-click="letter_action('prev')">{{prev_label}}</button><button class="btn narrow" data-event-click="letter_action('next')">{{next_label}}</button><button class="btn" data-event-click="letter_action('close')">{{close_label}}</button>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
